joedb provides CMake targets:

    find_package(joedb CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE joedb::joedb)

The `joedbc_build` helpers compile database schemas as part of your build.
Call `joedbc_build` with a schema directory relative to the current source
directory, then add the generated source file to your target:

    find_package(joedb CONFIG REQUIRED)
    include("${joedb_DIR}/joedbc_build.cmake")

    joedbc_build("src" database)

    add_executable(my_app main.cpp src/database/writable.cpp)
    target_include_directories(my_app PRIVATE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src")
    target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE joedb::joedb)

Use `joedbc_build_absolute` when the schema directory is an absolute path.

The schema directory should contain `database.joedbi` and `database.joedbc`.
The helper also handles schema inputs in a `database.rpc` subdirectory.
